<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Romulus Augustulus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">deposed <a href="/years/476">476 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> Augustulus was the last emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>, a youth placed on the throne by his father, the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a>. He was deposed in 476 CE by the Germanic commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a>, a date conventionally used to mark the end of Roman rule in the West. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> note that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s coronation in 800 created the first Western emperor since his deposition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="Romulus Augustulus" width="320" height="311" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ANS · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_Solidus_of_Romulus_Augustulus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…800 CE, Pope Leo III crowned Charlemagne in St. Peter's Basilica in Rome, where he was acclaimed Imperator Romanorum, making him the first emperor in the West since the deposition of <b>Romulus Augustulus</b> in 476 CE and establishing the ideal of a unified Christian Europe under Carolingian leadership.</blockquote><a href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>On 4 September 476 CE the Germanic commander Odoacer deposed <b>Romulus Augustulus</b>, the last Western emperor, and sent the imperial regalia to Constantinople, an act that contemporaries barely remarked upon, so gradual and complete had the erosion of Western Roman authority become.</blockquote><a href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>He was the first emperor in the West since the deposition of <b>Romulus Augustulus</b> in 476.</blockquote><a href="/essays/christmas-day-in-history">Christmas Day in History</a></li><li><blockquote>By the time Odoacer deposed the boy emperor <b>Romulus Augustulus</b> in 476, the western state had been shrinking for a generation into something closer to an Italian kingdom with an imperial title.</blockquote><a href="/essays/the-collapse-problem">The Collapse Problem</a></li><li><blockquote>Orestes then made his young son <b>Romulus Augustulus</b> emperor; he would be the last to rule in the West.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-28">28 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Germanic commander Odoacer deposed the boy emperor <b>Romulus Augustulus</b> and sent the imperial regalia to Constantinople.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-4">4 September in history</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pannonia">Pannonia</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=44.9,19.02&amp;year=476" aria-label="Pannonia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5003 578 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Romulus Augustulus"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5453 848h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5453 848h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=44.9,19.02&amp;year=476">What was here in 476 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
